tel 1.0 specification.tel/tels
name lira-guarantees

# The guarantee interchange format (builds.md §12.2): the build tool serializes the
# compiled cell's guaranteed presumption set to canonical BinTEL under this schema,
# and a tool's macros consult it to decide how to compile references — totally,
# where the class permits. Each entry carries its atom value hash and contract
# module so that consulting and recording are one act: the macro that compiles a
# total read also collects the atom it relied on, and the accumulated atoms become
# the release's uses blobs (lira-uses), grouped by module. Only configuration-class
# guarantees appear; admission-gate kinds never reach a compiler (builds.md §12.1).
#
# The file is an input to compilation, so its bytes are canonical: BinTEL canonical
# form, entries sorted by ascending atom hash, no duplicates — the lira-atoms
# precedent. It is the serialized form of the lira.tool Invocation's presumption
# set: in-process plugins receive the value directly; external compilers receive
# this file through an output-affecting setting.

scalar Hash
  description  A 256-bit BLAKE3 hash, BASE-256 encoded (32 characters)
  validate     base-256-hash

scalar ModuleName
  description  A LIRA module name (spec §14)
  validate     module-name

scalar TemporalClass
  description  lifetime or startup (builds.md §12.1)
  validate     temporal-class

# The class states what totality a macro may claim (builds.md §12.1's temporal
# classes, carried in-band so macros never hardcode discipline semantics):
# lifetime — holds for the whole process (envvars, datasets, isa);
# startup — verified at start, may lapse (files, tmpdir capacity aside).
record Guarantee
  description  One guaranteed presumption of the compiled cell

  field kind Identifier
  field name String
  field predicate String optional
  field class TemporalClass
  field module ModuleName
  field atom Hash

document
  field guarantee Guarantee optional repeatable  # ascending by atom hash; no duplicates
